* Low-dropout regulator: 5T error amplifier, PMOS pass device, RC load
* Eight coupled MOSFETs with every internal bias generated on chip. The loop
* is negative through p_pass: a rise at nfb pulls ea1 down, which drives eao
* up, which turns the pass device off. Line regulation is a supply sweep and
* load regulation a current step, matching the two measurements the retired
* AnalogGym LDO testbenches used. No .ic card anywhere.
<MODEL_SETUP>
.temp <TEMP>
Vdd vdd 0 <VDD>
Vref vref 0 <LDO_VREF>
Ibias vdd nbias <IBIAS_CELL>
<N_PREFIX>n_bias nbias nbias 0 0 <N_DEVICE>
<N_PREFIX>n_tail tail nbias 0 0 <N_DEVICE>
<N_PREFIX>n_fb ea1 nfb tail 0 <N_DEVICE>
<N_PREFIX>n_ref eao vref tail 0 <N_DEVICE>
<P_PREFIX>p_l ea1 ea1 vdd vdd <P_DEVICE>
<P_PREFIX>p_r eao ea1 vdd vdd <P_DEVICE>
<P_PREFIX>p_pass vout eao vdd vdd <P_DEVICE>
Rfb1 vout nfb <LDO_RFB1>
Rfb2 nfb 0 <LDO_RFB2>
Cout vout 0 <LDO_COUT>
Iload vout 0 <LDO_LOAD_SPEC>
<ANALYSIS>
.end
